1
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:39,840
[Abyss]

2
00:01:47,479 --> 00:01:48,320
[Operating Room]

3
00:02:09,050 --> 00:02:13,050
[Operating Room]

4
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:24,350
[Operating Room]

5
00:02:41,630 --> 00:02:46,450
[Episode 10]

6
00:02:54,300 --> 00:02:55,470
Come on, 3 to 7.

7
00:02:55,470 --> 00:02:56,470
6, 7, 8, 9, 10.

8
00:02:57,250 --> 00:02:58,250
Well, I've got...

9
00:02:58,870 --> 00:02:59,910
We're from
Huangshui Criminal Investigation Brigade.

10
00:02:59,910 --> 00:03:00,780
Zhang Chengguo.

11
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:00,490
[Public Security]

12
00:03:00,910 --> 00:03:01,860
Where were you

13
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:02,680
between 11:30 p.m. last night

14
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:04,280
and 12:30 a.m. this morning?

15
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:05,240
Me?

16
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:06,680
I've been working here

17
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:08,360
at the hotel since yesterday.

18
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,860
I-I was playing cards right here
last night.

19
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:11,030
W-What time did we start playing?

20
00:03:11,030 --> 00:03:12,190
A-After 9 p.m., I think.

21
00:03:12,190 --> 00:03:14,390
We started around 9 p.m. and never left.

22
00:03:14,530 --> 00:03:15,560
Ask them if you don't believe me.

23
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:16,930
Yeah, we've been playing cards here

24
00:03:16,930 --> 00:03:17,690
since after 9 p.m. last night.

25
00:03:17,690 --> 00:03:18,780
We weren't gambling—

26
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:20,280
just killing time.

27
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:22,829
Hand over your phone.

28
00:03:23,690 --> 00:03:24,840
M-My phone?

29
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:26,770
What else? Don't play dumb with me!

30
00:03:27,060 --> 00:03:27,680
But, Officer,

31
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:29,710
I-I lost my phone
the day before yesterday.

32
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:31,970
I even reported it to the police station.

33
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:34,150
Really, ask the police station
if you don't believe me.

34
00:03:34,150 --> 00:03:34,930
Lost it?

35
00:03:35,250 --> 00:03:36,450
Where did you lose it?

36
00:03:36,570 --> 00:03:38,490
H-How would I know? I...

37
00:03:38,590 --> 00:03:40,650
I still had it
the morning before yesterday.

38
00:03:40,650 --> 00:03:42,579
I was busy all morning
and didn't use it much.

39
00:03:42,579 --> 00:03:43,960
In the afternoon,
I checked my pocket and it was gone.

40
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:45,690
I-I couldn't find it anywhere.

41
00:03:45,750 --> 00:03:46,820
Really, I...

42
00:03:47,370 --> 00:03:48,579
I guess I might have

43
00:03:48,579 --> 00:03:49,520
accidentally left it somewhere,

44
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:50,800
and a guest took it.

45
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:54,940
Come with me to the police station
to assist with the investigation!

46
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:55,680
Let's go!

47
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:57,760
-Move!
-What is this about?

48
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:01,380
[Happiness Park]

49
00:04:01,460 --> 00:04:02,530
[Police]

50
00:04:19,170 --> 00:04:21,980
[Huangshui Public Security]

51
00:04:22,210 --> 00:04:23,430
What do you know?

52
00:04:23,850 --> 00:04:24,750
Spit it out.

53
00:04:25,430 --> 00:04:26,680
Last night,

54
00:04:27,090 --> 00:04:28,450
I got messages

55
00:04:28,450 --> 00:04:30,180
from both Zhang Chengguo and Han Pinmu
asking to meet me,

56
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:31,630
almost at the same time.

57
00:04:32,290 --> 00:04:33,320
As you know,

58
00:04:33,890 --> 00:04:35,640
we've always suspected that those two

59
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:37,440
were connected to the 3/12 Case,

60
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:40,570
so I figured I might be able
to get some clues from them.

61
00:04:40,570 --> 00:04:42,740
The meeting times they set
were very close,

62
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:44,140
so I discussed it with Master and decided

63
00:04:44,140 --> 00:04:45,800
that I'd go meet Han Pinmu first.

64
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,180
If I ran out of time,

65
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:49,430
he'd go meet Zhang Chengguo for me.

66
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:52,570
Wang Tao should have told you

67
00:04:52,570 --> 00:04:54,360
what happened next.

68
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:56,480
He was with me the whole time.

69
00:04:57,740 --> 00:04:59,740
Why didn't Zhao Ganzhe report this?

70
00:05:00,990 --> 00:05:03,190
I was worried about our safety too.

71
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:04,110
But Master said

72
00:05:04,130 --> 00:05:06,260
only a fool would go to a meeting alone.

73
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:08,860
I didn't realize until I got in the car

74
00:05:09,150 --> 00:05:10,950
that he'd had Wang Tao protect me

75
00:05:11,050 --> 00:05:12,910
while he went to the park himself.

76
00:05:14,010 --> 00:05:16,040
So he's that fool.

77
00:05:24,710 --> 00:05:26,610
What did Han Pinmu tell you?

78
00:05:29,970 --> 00:05:32,550
Hu Xiaofei was Feiyang.

79
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:35,150
They were good friends.

80
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:37,840
Hu Xiaofei had a secret,

81
00:05:38,390 --> 00:05:40,909
and he knew what it was,
but he wouldn't tell me.

82
00:05:40,909 --> 00:05:43,070
It's as if he's taunting us,

83
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:44,960
yet also beating around the bush.

84
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:47,390
Exactly, beating around the bush.

85
00:05:47,450 --> 00:05:49,890
We found a drink bottle

86
00:05:49,909 --> 00:05:51,970
near the scene where Zhao was killed.

87
00:05:52,830 --> 00:05:54,140
Han Pinmu's DNA

88
00:05:54,170 --> 00:05:55,930
was detected on it.

89
00:05:56,159 --> 00:05:57,490
How is that possible?

90
00:05:58,350 --> 00:05:59,500
When Master died,

91
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:00,900
Han Pinmu was clearly...

92
00:06:04,790 --> 00:06:05,750
I get it now.

93
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:08,300
Someone was trying to frame Han Pinmu,

94
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:09,310
and I ended up giving him

95
00:06:09,310 --> 00:06:10,830
an alibi.

96
00:06:12,010 --> 00:06:13,650
If he was able to predict this in advance,

97
00:06:13,650 --> 00:06:15,450
he must know who was behind this.

98
00:06:16,510 --> 00:06:18,470
Other than you and Wang Tao,

99
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:19,680
who else knew

100
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:22,160
Zhao was going to that meeting
in your place?

101
00:06:24,810 --> 00:06:25,750
No one.

102
00:06:27,170 --> 00:06:28,550
Did you arrest Zhang Chengguo?

103
00:06:28,550 --> 00:06:29,290
We did.

104
00:06:30,190 --> 00:06:33,040
But he has a rock-solid alibi.

105
00:06:35,510 --> 00:06:37,500
Who would want to kill Master?

106
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:41,659
Wait.

107
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:44,860
The text was sent to me.

108
00:06:45,730 --> 00:06:47,610
I was their target

109
00:06:48,340 --> 00:06:49,740
from the very beginning.

110
00:06:49,810 --> 00:06:52,050
If Han Pinmu knew in advance,

111
00:06:52,870 --> 00:06:54,260
he might have called you over

112
00:06:54,260 --> 00:06:56,050
to save you.

113
00:06:56,300 --> 00:06:58,250
But he never expected

114
00:06:58,420 --> 00:07:00,400
that Zhao would go in your place.

115
00:07:11,050 --> 00:07:12,910
You said you haven't used
your phone for 2 days.

116
00:07:12,910 --> 00:07:14,130
As a hotel manager,

117
00:07:14,190 --> 00:07:15,570
wasn't that inconvenient?

118
00:07:15,570 --> 00:07:17,300
Of course it was inconvenient.

119
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:19,320
But I figured,

120
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:21,430
what if the police station
found it for me?

121
00:07:21,430 --> 00:07:23,390
Then it would be a waste to get a new one.

122
00:07:23,390 --> 00:07:24,930
So I decided to wait a few more days.

123
00:07:24,930 --> 00:07:26,860
Why did you ask Li Cheng to meet you?

124
00:07:27,100 --> 00:07:28,830
I didn't ask Li Cheng to meet me.

125
00:07:29,330 --> 00:07:30,100
I lost my phone.

126
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:31,480
How could I have contacted him?

127
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:32,770
I didn't say anything.

128
00:07:32,790 --> 00:07:34,460
And I never said you contacted him
using your phone.

129
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:36,560
How did you know it was arranged
through your phone?

130
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:37,590
And how did you know

131
00:07:37,590 --> 00:07:39,720
it happened after you lost your phone?

132
00:07:42,020 --> 00:07:43,880
Answer the question.

133
00:07:44,630 --> 00:07:45,800
No, I...

134
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:47,630
I never asked Li Cheng to meet me.

135
00:07:47,630 --> 00:07:49,190
And I really did lose my phone.

136
00:07:49,190 --> 00:07:51,270
You... You kept asking me about it
just now,

137
00:07:51,270 --> 00:07:54,020
so... you know,
it was just a natural assumption.

138
00:07:54,050 --> 00:07:56,100
You can't just nitpick my words like that.

139
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:57,600
What's your relationship with Li Cheng?

140
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:59,120
My relationship with Li Cheng?

141
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:01,080
Just the kind where we say hello.

142
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:02,570
His mother, Sun Yuhua,

143
00:08:02,570 --> 00:08:04,360
works as a cleaner at our hotel.

144
00:08:04,390 --> 00:08:05,950
The kid's

145
00:08:05,950 --> 00:08:07,970
a good student, and he's polite.

146
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,360
I heard he was about to
be a police officer too,

147
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:13,060
so I guess you could say
he's the son of a colleague.

148
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:14,960
B-But it's not like we're close
or anything.

149
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:16,450
When was the last time

150
00:08:16,450 --> 00:08:17,480
you met Li Cheng?

151
00:08:19,510 --> 00:08:21,250
I... I can't remember clearly.

152
00:08:21,250 --> 00:08:22,130
Think.

153
00:08:24,660 --> 00:08:26,560
Well... that would be...

154
00:08:27,690 --> 00:08:30,000
I went to see him once after Song died.

155
00:08:30,020 --> 00:08:32,000
But that was to provide
you guys with clues.

156
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,260
You should have a record of it.

157
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:34,770
Do you know Zhao Ganzhe?

158
00:08:34,789 --> 00:08:35,409
Who?

159
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:36,650
Zhao Ganzhe,

160
00:08:36,679 --> 00:08:38,409
deputy captain
of our Criminal Investigation Brigade.

161
00:08:38,409 --> 00:08:39,240
The one who took your statement

162
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:40,289
when Song Laifu was killed.

163
00:08:40,289 --> 00:08:41,049
You forgot?

164
00:08:43,330 --> 00:08:44,940
Oh, Officer Zhao.

165
00:08:45,890 --> 00:08:47,750
I only saw him that one time.

166
00:08:47,770 --> 00:08:49,970
Does... Does that count as knowing him?

167
00:08:51,680 --> 00:08:52,410
Captain Fan.

168
00:08:52,560 --> 00:08:53,290
Captain Fan.

169
00:08:57,630 --> 00:08:58,630
How did it go?

170
00:08:58,650 --> 00:09:00,870
Manager Zhang answered every question
clearly and thoroughly.

171
00:09:00,870 --> 00:09:02,130
He was well-prepared.

172
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:04,650
What do you mean "well-prepared"?

173
00:09:04,690 --> 00:09:05,690
Come in.

174
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:21,260
Have a good talk with Manager Zhang.

175
00:09:22,750 --> 00:09:23,780
Li Cheng?

176
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,380
You seem surprised.

177
00:09:27,950 --> 00:09:28,920
I... I just didn't expect

178
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:30,220
to run into a colleague's kid

179
00:09:30,220 --> 00:09:31,340
here at the police station.

180
00:09:31,340 --> 00:09:33,270
It caught me off guard, that's all.

181
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:37,340
But then again, you're a police officer.

182
00:09:37,770 --> 00:09:39,340
Mrs. Sun must be proud.

183
00:09:39,410 --> 00:09:41,210
I only have one question for you.

184
00:09:41,890 --> 00:09:43,810
Do you know Han Pinmu?

185
00:09:43,930 --> 00:09:44,900
Han Pinmu?

186
00:09:47,290 --> 00:09:49,200
The name doesn't ring a bell.

187
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:50,690
Is he a hotel guest?

188
00:09:57,960 --> 00:09:59,530
Zhang Chengguo must be hiding something!

189
00:09:59,530 --> 00:10:01,080
I can see that.

190
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:04,010
But he definitely wasn't the one
who killed Zhao.

191
00:10:04,790 --> 00:10:05,770
We need to arrest Han Pinmu.

192
00:10:05,770 --> 00:10:07,410
He must know who did it.

193
00:10:07,410 --> 00:10:08,540
And on what grounds?

194
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:10,000
You think he'll confess?

195
00:10:10,010 --> 00:10:11,160
Forget Han Pinmu—

196
00:10:11,180 --> 00:10:12,720
once the detention period is up,
without evidence,

197
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:15,120
we'll even have to release Zhang Chengguo.

198
00:10:15,230 --> 00:10:17,250
The 3/12 Case happened 8 years ago.

199
00:10:17,380 --> 00:10:19,050
If Zhang Chengguo was
one of the perpetrators

200
00:10:19,050 --> 00:10:20,410
and hasn't committed any new crimes,

201
00:10:20,410 --> 00:10:21,550
how are we supposed to find evidence?

202
00:10:21,550 --> 00:10:23,250
We still have to find it.

203
00:10:23,790 --> 00:10:26,190
Or what? Are you suggesting
we use torture?

204
00:10:27,800 --> 00:10:28,790
I have to figure out

205
00:10:28,790 --> 00:10:30,340
exactly what Han Pinmu is thinking.

206
00:10:30,340 --> 00:10:32,390
If he and Zhang Chengguo
were accomplices back then,

207
00:10:32,390 --> 00:10:33,460
wouldn't he be worried
that if Zhang got arrested,

208
00:10:33,460 --> 00:10:34,750
he'd turn him in?

209
00:10:34,750 --> 00:10:36,210
Li Cheng, I'm warning you!

210
00:10:36,340 --> 00:10:37,580
You're just a witness here

211
00:10:37,580 --> 00:10:38,940
assisting with the investigation.

212
00:10:38,940 --> 00:10:41,000
This isn't your place to give orders!

213
00:10:41,040 --> 00:10:41,910
Finish your statement,

214
00:10:41,910 --> 00:10:43,820
go home, and wait to start your job!

215
00:10:43,820 --> 00:10:44,950
And I'm warning you,

216
00:10:45,020 --> 00:10:46,240
I'm not like Zhao.

217
00:10:46,270 --> 00:10:47,120
Without permission,

218
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:48,840
you're absolutely forbidden from
meeting with Han Pinmu privately.

219
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:49,980
If I find out you've done that,

220
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:51,890
you can forget about ever
becoming a police officer.

221
00:10:51,890 --> 00:10:52,700
Is that clear?

222
00:10:57,010 --> 00:10:57,940
Got it.

223
00:11:02,860 --> 00:11:03,750
Li Cheng.

224
00:11:05,150 --> 00:11:06,750
I hope you understand

225
00:11:07,870 --> 00:11:09,800
that I'm doing this to protect you.

226
00:11:10,980 --> 00:11:12,720
I know Zhao promised

227
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:15,210
to get you onto the task force.

228
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:18,720
I'll definitely help him make that happen.

229
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:21,310
Be patient, young man.

230
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:25,840
You'll get your chance to be
part of the investigation.

231
00:11:27,110 --> 00:11:28,440
Thank you, Captain Fan.

232
00:11:29,210 --> 00:11:31,270
Go see Hu Sen and sign your statement,

233
00:11:32,370 --> 00:11:33,770
then get some good sleep.

234
00:11:34,570 --> 00:11:35,450
Captain Fan,

235
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:38,570
I have a request.

236
00:11:40,520 --> 00:11:46,070
♪ The sun has dried the color
from my youthful face ♪

237
00:11:47,830 --> 00:11:53,530
♪ Whether in silence or crying out,
it all fades away with time ♪

238
00:11:55,810 --> 00:12:01,390
♪ What is this ache
that still lingers in my heart? ♪

239
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:09,270
♪ Reminding me that I don't deserve
to come through this unscathed ♪

240
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:10,500
There was a struggle.

241
00:12:12,710 --> 00:12:15,710
He tried to wrestle the knife away
from the assailant.

242
00:12:17,340 --> 00:12:20,050
♪ How many times must I get it wrong? ♪

243
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:24,450
♪ To make a lie come true ♪

244
00:12:32,830 --> 00:12:35,740
♪ How far must we go ♪

245
00:12:36,850 --> 00:12:38,830
♪ Before we can reach the truth? ♪

246
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:42,640
♪ How long can the years stretch on? ♪

247
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:46,510
♪ From childhood to old age ♪

248
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:50,340
♪ Those who are trapped can only ♪

249
00:12:51,230 --> 00:12:53,810
♪ Keep searching, day after day ♪

250
00:12:54,650 --> 00:12:57,600
♪ How fleeting life is ♪

251
00:12:58,530 --> 00:13:01,240
♪ From first meeting to farewell ♪

252
00:13:02,260 --> 00:13:05,280
♪ I refuse to forgive, because that is ♪

253
